\begin{beyond}
\textbf{Taken on trust: these are all the oscillator states.} The argument above shows, at the heuristic level of the tail comparison, that a nonterminating series gives a non-normalizable $\psi$. That no other energies give bound states, and that the functions $H_{n-1}(x)e^{-x^2/2}$ form a complete orthogonal set, is a theorem whose careful proof can be found in \cite{griffiths} and \cite{rhb}; we take it on trust.
\end{beyond}
